  "submitted_text": "Step 1: Start by simplifying the left side of the equation \\(2^3 \\cdot 3^x = 72\\).\n\nStep 2: Calculate \\(2^3\\), which equals 8. So the equation becomes \\(8 \\cdot 3^x = 72\\).\n\nStep 3: Divide both sides of the equation by 8 to isolate \\(3^x\\). This gives \\(3^x = \\frac{72}{8}\\).\n\nStep 4: Simplify the right side of the equation, \\(\\frac{72}{8} = 9\\). So the equation now is \\(3^x = 9\\).\n\nStep 5: Recognize that 9 can be written as \\(3^2\\). Therefore, the equation becomes \\(3^x = 3^2\\).\n\nStep 6: Since the bases are the same, set the exponents equal to each other, giving \\(x = 2\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{2}",
